WEBVTT

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:34.450
<b>Holmes of Kyoto</b>

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:50.580
Episode 10

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:50.580
"The Bisque Doll's Smile"

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:55.460
<b>Happy New Year</b>

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:58.090
Good morning!

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:00.340
Hey, Aoi-chan.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:02.970
Happy New Year to all of you!

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:06.720
Happy New Year to you!

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:09.980
Happy New Year, Aoi-san.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.990
Wearing kimonos for our 
first day back to work...

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:15.480
This really has that Kura vibe!

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:18.110
Even though mine is 
the more informal version.

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:19.850
It really suits you.

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:21.600
Yours suits you as well, Aoi-san.

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:24.740
It certainly does. 
You look positively radiant.

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:28.120
Th-Thank you very much.

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:32.880
Heya! Sorry I'm late.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:35.380
Nobody even invited you.

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:38.130
The owner invited me!

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:44.390
Well, now that Akihito-kun's here,

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:45.690
we can begin.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:57.400
Takeshi, Kiyotaka...

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:59.120
Yoshie, Aoi-chan...

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:01.080
Rikyu, Akihito-kun...

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.040
Let's toast to another year together.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.160
Cheers!

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:06.130
Cheers!

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:10.300
I'm gonna make you fall for me, Yoshie-san!

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:12.070
I'm flattered.

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:13.790
Give me a break...

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:17.890
Your writing still don't 
got enough depth to it...

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:20.300
I can't win with you, Dad...

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.980
I guess you can even dress up a peasant.

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:25.770
How dare you, Rikyu?

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:28.560
Aoi-san is hardly a peasant!

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:31.540
Don't be so mad, Kiyo-nii!

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:34.010
Anyway, we're headin' out on a date.

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:36.570
He's going to take me somewhere nice.

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:40.890
Excuse me, but would you mind 
waiting a bit before heading out?

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:43.110
It's our first day at work in the new year,

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:46.580
and I'd like to take Aoi-san to Yata Jizo Son.

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:49.550
Sure, but make it quick.

00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:50.450
We ain't waitin' long.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.650
All right, Aoi-san. Let's go.

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:55.620
I'll tag along!

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:56.030
Me too!

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:57.340
Hold on just a minute, now.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:02.180
Akihito-kun, Rikyu, you leave those two be.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:07.100
The boy wants to walk around town 
with Aoi-chan in their kimonos.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:13.160
Kiyotaka, if you don't 
tell others how you feel,

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:14.440
they'll never know.

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:21.610
<b>Yata Jizo Son</b>

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:29.520
<i>Please help me learn to drink the 
black coffee that Holmes-san makes!</i>

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:34.280
You seem to be wishing
 rather hard for something.

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:37.660
It must be something wonderful.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:44.400
Let's have another fine 
year together, all right?

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.900
That sounds great.

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:48.890
I hope you'll teach me
 all kinds of things this year.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:53.890
Teach you? What in particular 
do you want to learn?

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:56.400
What do I want...?

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:11.540
No... We can't, Holmes-san...

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:17.210
Can't what?

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:19.730
Oh, I didn't mean...

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:24.050
I-I want to learn more 
about R-Raku tea bowls!

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:25.800
Raku tea bowls?

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:26.680
Yes!

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:32.270
It was so frustrating at the party,
not being able to tell if they were real...

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:34.030
I see.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:37.130
I understand feeling frustrated.

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:41.320
I'll teach you all about Raku tea bowls
 while you're on winter break.

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:43.320
Please do!

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.680
Well, the owner is waiting.

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:47.070
Shall we return to the store?

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:47.870
Sure.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:57.330
By the way, are the owner 
and Yoshie-san not married?

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:03.650
My grandfather divorced my grandmother for
 personal reasons when my father was young.

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:06.590
Because of that, they've decided 
not to make it official.

00:06:07.850 --> 00:06:09.590
<i>What reasons could that be?</i>

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:14.550
While we're out, would you 
like to get some coffee here?

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:16.980
But isn't the owner waiting for us?

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:19.390
He can wait a bit longer.

00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:22.350
Hey, come on... We really should get back.

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:24.470
Don't look so sad!

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:27.860
You can take me some other time.

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:30.030
To any cafe you recommend!

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:34.240
All right. I'll invite you soon, then.

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:36.500
Well then...

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:38.560
Shall we head out now?

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:43.880
Can I take you up on your offer to go
 with me to a cafe of my recommending?

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:45.380
Oh, sure!

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:47.350
I'm so glad.

00:06:47.350 --> 00:06:51.160
I was a little hesitant to go by myself.

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:54.180
<i>Oh, is that what this is about?</i>

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:02.150
It's charming!

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:04.500
The atmosphere inside should be nice, too.

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:08.700
Wow!

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:10.500
The first floor is a chocolaterie.

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:12.600
The cafe is in the basement.

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:13.660
Here.

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:20.160
That's the entrance.

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:29.410
"Angel Library"? What does that mean?

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:35.000
They say the angels who study hard every day 
to make delicious chocolate for everyone

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:38.320
converted their own library into a cafe

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:42.100
so that the customers could relax 
in a more leisurely atmosphere.

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:46.570
If you would, punch in this 
code to open the door.

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:49.220
This is kind of exciting!

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:06.810
It's so wonderful, my heart is pounding!

00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:09.210
I'm so glad you like it.

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:11.220
Here you are.

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:13.280
Do you need a fresh?

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:15.130
No, thank you.

00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:16.220
Ma'am?

00:08:21.130 --> 00:08:23.730
<i>What's a "fresh"?</i>

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:26.230
<i>Some kind of fruit dish?</i>

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:29.480
I'm sure you don't need 
a fresh anymore, Aoi-san.

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:33.110
Did you think I needed one?

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:38.120
No, not now that you're 
trying to be an adult.

00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:40.840
Um, Holmes-san...

00:08:40.840 --> 00:08:41.810
What is it?

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:44.120
What's a fresh?

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:47.400
Of course...

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:50.630
You wouldn't know what a fresh is.

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:53.410
Forgive my ignorance, but...

00:08:53.410 --> 00:08:58.010
It's something that people 
trying to be adults don't need?

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:00.510
So it's got nothing to do with fruit, then?

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:02.120
No.

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:04.890
I think you might understand 
once you try your coffee.

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:12.530
This is my first time drinking black coffee.

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:14.400
It's kind of unnerving...

00:09:21.070 --> 00:09:23.910
It's a little bitter for my tastes.

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:27.560
Then why not ask for a fresh?

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:32.550
In Kansai, coffee with milk 
is referred to as a fresh.

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:39.060
<i>Holmes-san... a real nasty Kyoto boy.</i>

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:44.930
I managed to drink it without sugar.

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:47.560
You're one step closer to adulthood.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:48.880
That reminds me...

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:52.590
You said you were hesitant 
to come to this cafe by yourself.

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:55.570
Do you usually visit cafes alone?

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:58.570
Well, I don't have anyone else to go with.

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:02.480
There's not a girl 
you could ask to go with you?

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:05.830
Maybe a girl you'd like as a girlfriend?

00:10:09.610 --> 00:10:10.940
I don't really know.

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:14.710
I've never particularly wanted a girlfriend.

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:18.590
I was flattered when Izumi asked me out,

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:22.470
and I was curious about dating, so I accepted...

00:10:22.670 --> 00:10:24.880
But that ended in disaster,

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:28.480
so I've kept my distance 
from relationships ever since.

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:30.010
I see...

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:34.110
But lately, I've begun to 
think that spending my days

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:36.860
with a girlfriend might not be so bad.

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:42.870
That it might be nice to have 
someone to spend time with.

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:46.720
<i>Holmes-san has fallen for someone...</i>

00:10:48.550 --> 00:10:49.400
Aoi-san?

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:51.160
R-Right.

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:52.640
I see.

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:54.780
Yes, I see...

00:10:54.780 --> 00:10:57.880
If you brought her to this cafe,  
I bet she'd fall head over heels!

00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:00.860
Head over heels, you say?

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:06.700
Oh, Kiyotaka!

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:09.640
Grandma!

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:11.300
<i>Grandma?!</i>

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:14.270
My, haven't you grown!

00:11:15.470 --> 00:11:18.880
Um, I'm a part-timer at Kura.

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:20.670
My name is Mashiro Aoi.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:23.990
A pleasure to meet ya.

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:27.410
<i>If this is his grandmother...</i>

00:11:27.730 --> 00:11:32.790
<i>My grandfather divorced my grandmother for
 personal reasons when my father was young.</i>

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:36.170
<i>She's the owner's ex-wife 
that Holmes-san mentioned before?</i>

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:37.910
Say, Kiyotaka,

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:40.240
since we've run into each other,

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:42.380
why don't you stop by my place?

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:45.200
Oh, but I don't even have 
anything to bring you...

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:46.830
Don't you worry about that.

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:49.180
Aoi-san, would you like to join us?

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:51.020
Yes, I'd love to.

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:53.940
<b>Watanabe</b>

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:57.660
I appreciated the birthday flowers
 you sent me last month.

00:11:57.660 --> 00:11:58.570
It was nothing.

00:11:58.850 --> 00:12:03.200
Seiji-san went and sent me
 flowers this year, too.

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:04.710
Grandfather did?

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:06.580
Yoshio-san.

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:11.200
I ran into Kiyotaka in front 
of the chocolate shop.

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:12.770
It's good to see you again.

00:12:12.770 --> 00:12:14.600
Hello! I'm Mashiro Aoi.

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:21.170
He's awful shy.

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:26.600
So, Kiyotaka,

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:31.570
Seiji-san said something about it 
in the letter he sent with his flowers...

00:12:31.570 --> 00:12:34.480
Are you still playin' detective?

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:37.920
I hardly think of myself 
as playing detective...

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:39.480
Why? Has something happened?

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:41.590
Wait here a moment.

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:47.860
It's about this.

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:55.000
<b>Watanabe</b>

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.750
Have you made the connection?

00:13:01.750 --> 00:13:03.330
Y-Yes.

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:08.390
This bisque doll is the boy counterpart
to the girl doll in the store, isn't it?

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:09.760
Yes.

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:14.420
When we were first married, 
Seiji-san bought this pair of dolls.

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:19.000
After we divorced, he sent me my things.

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:22.090
The boy doll was among them.

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:24.400
Is there something wrong 
with the bisque doll?

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:28.910
My granddaughter who lives nearby
 is sayin' it scares her.

00:13:29.340 --> 00:13:31.400
Well, it is a little scary...

00:13:31.400 --> 00:13:33.910
She only recently started saying that?

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:39.800
You see, I'd been keepin' it
 on a shelf in my room.

00:13:40.360 --> 00:13:43.670
But I recently thought of it 
and put it out in the living room.

00:13:45.560 --> 00:13:48.720
At first, my granddaughter said it was cute,

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:52.930
but lately, she's started sayin' it's creepy.
 That it's cursed, even.

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:54.310
Cursed?

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:58.030
That's right. My granddaughter
 said she found it cryin'.

00:14:01.910 --> 00:14:03.140
I see...

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:13.950
She said she thought 
she heard someone weepin'.

00:14:14.190 --> 00:14:17.210
An' when she opened the living room door...

00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:19.460
She found the doll lyin' on the floor,

00:14:19.730 --> 00:14:22.840
its eyes wet with tears.

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:29.970
Since then, the doll's been movin'. 
From the sofa to the piano an' all around...

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:31.740
I-It moves?

00:14:32.190 --> 00:14:34.350
What do you think, Kiyotaka?

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:35.900
Let me think...

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:41.610
Was it last month that you 
took the doll off your shelf?

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:43.980
Yes, around the end of the year.

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:47.490
And your granddaughter visits 
your house frequently?

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:50.490
She's been stoppin' by often
 over winter vacation.

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:53.990
Does the doll only move on days 
your granddaughter is visiting?

00:14:54.320 --> 00:14:58.250
Yes, I'd say so, actually.

00:14:58.460 --> 00:15:00.310
Is it a ghost?

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:06.000
I was wonderin' if I ought 
to be callin' an exorcist...

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:07.990
It's not possessed.

00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:11.010
I believe this is a man-made phenomenon.

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:13.920
A man-made phenomenon?

00:15:13.920 --> 00:15:16.140
You mean someone here is doin' it?

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:17.620
Holmes-san...

00:15:24.740 --> 00:15:29.280
Grandmother, why did you 
take the doll off the shelf?

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:33.280
Why? Well, I just started 
feelin' nostalgic about it.

00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:38.660
Might that be because of
 the flowers Grandfather sent you?

00:15:38.850 --> 00:15:42.350
Why, yes. The flowers got me 
thinkin' about old times,

00:15:42.350 --> 00:15:44.670
so I brought the doll out, too.

00:15:45.030 --> 00:15:46.780
Just to be certain,

00:15:46.780 --> 00:15:50.590
had you ever told anyone 
that the bisque doll

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:53.800
was from Grandfather before then?

00:15:55.690 --> 00:15:56.680
Oh...

00:15:57.110 --> 00:15:59.680
No, I don't suppose I had.

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:02.460
Grandfather sent you those 
flowers for your birthday,

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:05.140
then you put that doll in the living room.

00:16:05.740 --> 00:16:08.790
Did your husband inquire about it?

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:10.920
He sure did.

00:16:10.920 --> 00:16:14.320
"Gettin' those flowers from Seiji-san 
reminded me," I told him.

00:16:15.860 --> 00:16:16.670
Nice, eh?

00:16:18.050 --> 00:16:23.080
"This doll was a present from him as well."

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:26.390
Could I see it?

00:16:27.740 --> 00:16:28.210
Yes.

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:33.970
I wonder if your husband was 
quite shocked to learn that

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:40.220
the doll you've treasured for so long 
was a gift from Grandfather.

00:16:40.910 --> 00:16:42.230
Shocked?

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:45.100
I heard that the reason you 
and Grandfather split up

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:48.720
was because you fell badly ill 
shortly after you were married

00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:53.110
and he thought that he had
 cursed you somehow.

00:16:53.370 --> 00:16:55.110
Cursed her?

00:16:55.320 --> 00:16:58.480
I heard that a shaman told him this:

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:03.740
"You are haunted by bad karma.

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:05.860
It won't harm you personally,

00:17:05.860 --> 00:17:09.020
but instead will afflict your spouse."

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:14.630
It was a total sham, of course.

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:18.380
But as your illness continued to linger,

00:17:18.380 --> 00:17:20.690
Grandfather made up his mind to leave.

00:17:22.120 --> 00:17:27.270
I wonder if he sent the boy doll
 to stay with you in his place,

00:17:28.010 --> 00:17:31.900
and kept the girl doll as a token of you.

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:35.650
"I can't be your husband anymore,

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:37.630
but I still wanted to be with you."

00:17:38.550 --> 00:17:41.790
I wonder if that was the 
meaning behind the gift.

00:17:42.220 --> 00:17:46.590
I'm sure such a message would have resonated
with your current husband more than anyone.

00:17:51.910 --> 00:17:56.100
But I was married to Seiji-san
 for only five years,

00:17:56.100 --> 00:17:58.680
and I've been with Yoshio-san for fifty.

00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:02.840
Yes. I'm sure your husband has believed in you,

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:05.440
but this was a brief blow to that faith.

00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:12.440
"Perhaps all this time, I've just
 been a replacement for Seiji-san."

00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:17.060
"Maybe she's been thinking of Seiji-san 
the entire time we've been together."

00:18:17.060 --> 00:18:18.070
Oh no...

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:20.950
Assaulted by a wave of such feelings,

00:18:21.520 --> 00:18:24.400
it's quite natural that he'd start to cry.

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:31.520
That's when he heard your 
granddaughter's footsteps.

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:36.030
He quickly set the doll down and fled.

00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:40.090
The doll, left on the floor,

00:18:40.090 --> 00:18:43.350
may have been wet with your husband's tears.

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:48.730
So you think he's been movin' the doll?

00:18:49.610 --> 00:18:52.790
Perhaps hearing your granddaughter
 say the doll was scary

00:18:53.260 --> 00:18:56.840
inspired dark ideas in your husband's mind.

00:18:57.980 --> 00:19:01.930
By moving it around, he thought, 
you might come to find it unsettling as well,

00:19:01.930 --> 00:19:05.560
and return it to the Yagashira family.

00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:08.200
Holmes-san, that's going too far...

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:10.320
I've been such a fool.

00:19:11.320 --> 00:19:15.000
I'm only now realizing how Seiji-san felt.

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:19.130
And I've hurt the person

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:23.290
who's stayed with me and 
treasured me all this time...

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:34.520
Kiyotaka, would you mind takin' 
this little fellow to Kura?

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:38.150
Of course. We'll take good care of him.

00:19:39.800 --> 00:19:43.520
Get along with your sweetheart 
at Kiyotaka's place, all right?

00:19:46.300 --> 00:19:51.620
Kiyotaka, Aoi-san... You should always 
be honest about how you feel, too.

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:55.630
R-Right!

00:19:56.110 --> 00:19:57.820
You especially, Kiyotaka.

00:19:57.820 --> 00:20:01.170
You never speak up 
when you want somethin'.

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:03.890
You need to tell people these things.

00:20:04.100 --> 00:20:05.560
That's true.

00:20:05.560 --> 00:20:10.270
I always thought that if I didn't say I 
wanted something, it wouldn't hurt to lose it.

00:20:10.510 --> 00:20:16.020
As a result, I've been unable to say 
I wanted something, even when I truly do.

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:18.390
You're such a fool.

00:20:18.390 --> 00:20:22.450
It's much more painful to lose something' 
because you didn't speak up.

00:20:23.650 --> 00:20:25.190
You got that right.

00:20:25.190 --> 00:20:27.870
You never know yourself,

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:30.200
but you sure do know me.

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:33.720
Well, that's 'cause I'm your grandma!

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:44.710
Come visit us again sometime.

00:20:44.710 --> 00:20:45.470
Sure!

00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:47.100
Oh!

00:20:48.460 --> 00:20:49.850
That doll...

00:20:50.240 --> 00:20:54.130
Yes, we're going to take it to Kura.

00:20:56.730 --> 00:21:00.200
Oh, I've been wantin' to return 
it for the longest time.

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:01.940
Today was the perfect opportunity.

00:21:02.550 --> 00:21:03.610
You sure?

00:21:05.630 --> 00:21:10.560
I was hopin' you'd buy me a new doll, dear.

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:14.740
If that's what you want, all right.

00:21:18.600 --> 00:21:21.770
The girl at Kura is probably 
waiting to see him.

00:21:21.770 --> 00:21:23.260
I'm sure she is.

00:21:24.060 --> 00:21:26.900
After all, it's been fifty years.

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:38.900
<i>They look so happy!</i>

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:41.020
<i>Holmes-san...</i>

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:47.010
Is something the matter, Aoi-san?

00:21:47.010 --> 00:21:49.410
Huh? Oh, no, nothing.

00:21:49.690 --> 00:21:53.290
They really do look happy to be together.

00:21:56.290 --> 00:21:59.290
You're right... They look very happy.

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:14.290
<b>Holmes of Kyoto</b>

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:51.380
Next Episode

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:51.380
"Valentine's Party"

00:23:37.160 --> 00:23:38.330
It's Valentine's Day.

00:23:38.330 --> 00:23:40.580
Should I give out some handmade chocolates?

00:23:40.580 --> 00:23:41.990
It's February 14th, so...

00:23:41.990 --> 00:23:45.060
I w-w-wasn't doing anything!

00:23:45.060 --> 00:23:47.570
Next time: "Valentine's Party."

00:23:47.570 --> 00:23:50.410
H-Holmes-san, you really are nasty.
